{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496753-bodhisattva-predator-arcana-werewolves","id":1496753,"title":"Bodhisattva Predator: Arcana Werewolves","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-10T16:10:59-08:00","id":1496753,"title":"Bodhisattva Predator: Arcana Werewolves","content":"In The Sundered World it is revealed that all Pangeans, including Father/Mother Wolf (and possibly the Firstborn), possess Arcana as they are Pillars of the World and are able warp reality in certain ways. As shards of the Lord of Wolves, would Uratha who grew strong enough (perhaps by reaching some ascended state similar to Mage: TAW's Archemages) be able to unlock limited facets of Arcana or is it just simply beyond them? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27672-forsakenprospects","name":"ForsakenProspects","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27672_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-11T06:22:08-08:00","id":1496797,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d say no. They\u2019re not Pangaeans at full power, but halfbreeds whose blood has run thinner over the ages. No, Gifts and rites, for Uratha.<br /> <br /> Now, should bodhisattva predators get powers unique to themselves? I\u2019d say yes, but nothing common. Each would have a unique power only that bodhisattva predator possesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-11T06:48:52-08:00","id":1496800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ForsakenProspects</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496753-bodhisattva-predator-arcana-werewolves#post1496753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As shards of the Lord of Wolves</div> </div> </div> </div>They are not shards of Wolf.<br /> <br /> In fact, they might not be descendants at all; rather Uratha might just created in Wolf's own image.<br /> <br /> Regardless, since literal shards of Pangaeans (the Hosts) haven't exhibited the ability to use the Arcana, werewolves are extremely unlikely to do so barring some extremely weird and unique circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-11-2022, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-11T06:53:20-08:00","id":1496801,"title":"","content":"I agree. I would not allow Uratha to learn Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-11T07:04:29-08:00","id":1496804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496753-bodhisattva-predator-arcana-werewolves?p=1496797#post1496797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d say no. They\u2019re not Pangaeans at full power, but halfbreeds whose blood has run thinner over the ages. No, Gifts and rites, for Uratha.<br /> <br /> Now, should bodhisattva predators get powers unique to themselves? I\u2019d say yes, but nothing common. Each would have a unique power only that bodhisattva predator possesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shunned by the Moon listed (some) the powers that bodhisattva predators out to have, I quote &quot;Enlightenments are mimicries of the power of the legendary bodhisattva predators&quot; so we already know what the powers are... But not the real requirements to get them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-11T07:33:06-08:00","id":1496807,"title":"","content":"To those of us without that supplement, what <i>are</i> those powers? I\u2019m not asking for a full writeup, just a generalized idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-11T11:33:47-08:00","id":1496836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496753-bodhisattva-predator-arcana-werewolves?p=1496797#post1496797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d say no. They\u2019re not Pangaeans at full power, but halfbreeds whose blood has run thinner over the ages. No, Gifts and rites, for Uratha.<br /> <br /> Now, should bodhisattva predators get powers unique to themselves? I\u2019d say yes, but nothing common. Each would have a unique power only that bodhisattva predator possesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is it stated their blood is thinning over time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-11T11:39:49-08:00","id":1496837,"title":"","content":"So, ignoring a lot of the side commentary, and going at it as a broad idea, and particularly in a crossover context, I wouldn't strictly say no to allowing a werewolf to gain access to a single Arcana that rise with Primal Urge starting at 6.<br /> <br /> Buuuuuuuuuuuut if we we wanna talk about why it's infeasible, we should probably address the reasons why it's &quot;Probably not.&quot;<br /> <br /> Reason 1) THe Pangaeans were just on a whole 'nother scale.<br /> <br /> One of the problems of Second Edition having it's lists of scales be so prominent, and in particular having four of it's most frequent entities sharing one scale in particular, is that it can be tempting to think that a lot of things are just comparable to each other when that's strictly not the case. A <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=857671#post857671\">Rank 5 Pangaean</a>* makes other Rank 5 Ephemeral entities look like chumps, and Pangaeans don't go lower than 3. Werewolves are beasts in their own right, god-killing demigods all of them, but the scale between them and where Wolf was at (particularly derived from understanding their peers, Bird and Snake) is vast enough to make one wonder.<br /> <br /> Reason 2) The metaphysical makeup works against them.<br /> <br /> One thing about the Pangaeans that is of a side note is that, in addition to walking the entire breadth of Flesh, Border Marches, and Shadow (well, would walk if it weren't for Wolf, and often in spite of them), Pangaeans also could dive into and connect with the Astral-and while there's no direct metaphysic that says the Astral is needed for employing the Supernal, it's worth noting that when the Arcana are expressed <i>as</i> Arcana, it's often throguh entitites who have connection to the Astral-it's a relationship we don't really see through the Shadow, Hedge, or Underworld through all but the wibbliest (and often questionably canon, given the state of second edition) of ways. Now, the Uratha aren't <i>divorced</i> from the Astral, the Cahalith regularly take advantage of the Dreaming Earth and Mother's Land with their dream abilities, and certain other gifts and Lodges breach it-but it's a strained relationship that implies that it would take more than just raw might of Primal Urge to do, you'd have to deliberately dig and <i>change</i> to really make that happen, partly because<br /> <br /> Reason 3) Werewolves are only part Pangaean.<br /> <br /> So on top of that gap between werewolves and Pangaeans, werewolves aren't commonly asserted to be pure Pangaean. The origin story they have implies that they're more a hybrid of Wolf and Humanity, with design input from Luna. So that adds a layer of divide all the more. But wait, wouldn't that added bit of humanity possibly mean they'd still have some kind of ability to tap into the Supernal? No, not really, since it possibly introduces a vector for the Lie to work on werewolves ala that shard of the abyss (Not enough to not make them sleepwalkers, but enough to be a barrier) and the access to the Supernal is implied to be an aspect of nature of the Pangaeans that this world simply doesn't have, and werewolves probably didn't have even at the time.<br /> <br /> There are probably other reasonable reasons to not really think of it like that.<br /> <br /> I dunno, I feel like if it were a really viable option, it'd probably have been mentioned in the Era-it's a pretty short enough mechanic to introduce so long as you cheat, and while most people don't play at the end of the power pool, it certainly would be more viable there than anywhere else. My go-to is, and remains, asserting that werewolves on the upper end of the Primal Urge tend to take on the Lone Wolf Template from the Chronicler's Guide-but I could see some games where this'd be a fun way to go about it to, and I wouldn't even bat at an eye at an obscure Lodge trying to explore the idea with limited results. But on the general vibe of the thing, I'd have to lean towards Nah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496753-bodhisattva-predator-arcana-werewolves?p=1496804#post1496804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shunned by the Moon listed (some) the powers that bodhisattva predators out to have, I quote &quot;Enlightenments are mimicries of the power of the legendary bodhisattva predators&quot; so we already know what the powers are... But not the real requirements to get them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't regard the Cull as the most reliable source of information for what a Bodhisattva Predator looks like, not gonna lie.<br /> <br /> \u200b*Oh by the way, the thread from there on will help you get some ideas, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12219\" data-vbnamecard=\"12219\">Demigod Beast</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-11-2022, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-11T15:35:46-08:00","id":1496861,"title":"","content":"I mentioned &quot;weird and unique circumstances&quot; earlier. I think it's far more likely (if extremely rare to the point where it might not have happened at all even if it's possible) that a werewolf would gain access to an Arcanum through their general mutability (especially Ghost Wolves) as well as their connection to the Anima Mundi. A werewolf who learns to dream lucidly and to explore Astral Space could possibly encounter the Aeons, and (potentially by forming a lodge around one) pick up part of their nature and Resonances into her own. Not to mention that the Aeons can grant use of spells from their associated Arcanum to mages. Who's to say they can't do it with non-mages?<br /> <br /> Or, as I realise right now, it's also possible to just have a lesser Supernal entity for a pack or lodge totem without having to navigate the far reaches of the Astral. Totems do affect those who are bound to them, though normally not to the point where they grant powers associated with other splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-11T17:10:17-08:00","id":1496868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496753-bodhisattva-predator-arcana-werewolves?p=1496837#post1496837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't regard the Cull as the most reliable source of information for what a Bodhisattva Predator looks like, not gonna lie[/USER]</div> </div> </div> </div>So what does a Bodhisttava Predator actually look like? We know what an Archmage looks like and there are some examples, both official and house ruled on the Vampire forum, of Kindred Elders but I can't really find anything on truly high end Uratha. For how inconvenient the dietary and spiritual needs of a Primal Urge 10 werewolf are, I would thing they would get a more substantial power up than 'heal 6 bashing/lethal plus the usual stat modifiers.'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27672-forsakenprospects","name":"ForsakenProspects","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27672_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-11T18:14:27-08:00","id":1496871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496753-bodhisattva-predator-arcana-werewolves?p=1496807#post1496807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To those of us without that supplement, what <i>are</i> those powers? I\u2019m not asking for a full writeup, just a generalized idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of them initially showed up as Enlightenments in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/798541-alpha-predators-the-strongest-werewolves?p=801351#post801351\">Chris Allen's writeup of Lycaon-Ur as a werewolf</a>. Others include being able to run tirelessly at the speed of the day's change (in practical terms, this translates to about a thousand miles per hour), negate any impediment to getting your teeth into an enemy, or come back from the dead fully healed once per scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-11T18:45:13-08:00","id":1496874,"title":"","content":"Ooooooo, I likely! Will we ever get official rules for 2e, though? Because the werewolf equivalent of archmasters is too cool to resist!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-12T10:29:42-08:00","id":1496920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496753-bodhisattva-predator-arcana-werewolves?p=1496871#post1496871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of them initially showed up as Enlightenments in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/798541-alpha-predators-the-strongest-werewolves?p=801351#post801351\">Chris Allen's writeup of Lycaon-Ur as a werewolf</a>. Others include being able to run tirelessly at the speed of the day's change (in practical terms, this translates to about a thousand miles per hour), negate any impediment to getting your teeth into an enemy, or come back from the dead fully healed once per scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly what I was looking for! <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27672-forsakenprospects","name":"ForsakenProspects","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27672_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-12T17:58:23-08:00","id":1496950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ForsakenProspects</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496753-bodhisattva-predator-arcana-werewolves?p=1496868#post1496868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what does a Bodhisttava Predator actually look like? We know what an Archmage looks like and there are some examples, both official and house ruled on the Vampire forum, of Kindred Elders but I can't really find anything on truly high end Uratha. For how inconvenient the dietary and spiritual needs of a Primal Urge 10 werewolf are, I would thing they would get a more substantial power up than 'heal 6 bashing/lethal plus the usual stat modifiers.'</div> </div> </div> </div>It's deliberately obscure.<br /> <br /> The idea of the &quot;Bodhisattva Predator&quot; is not a scalable thing, particularly since &quot;bodhisattva predator&quot; is legitimately <i>not</i> a game term, but instead a very illustrative term that people have grasped onto to as an icon to ask answers for-and-from. The phrase is...............not on the same scale as the way the God-Machine was demanded prior to 2nd Edition and Demon, but it's about comparably below on that scale. It's a thing the fandom latched onto, is what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> There have been teases that there might be more to the idea of an enlightened threshold-dwelling hunter-leader-liberator than simply references, but there is a lot of irony in the statement already, particularly since part of the reason Uratha elders aren't given the same space as vampire Elders or Mage Masters (let along archmasters) is because most Uratha tend to die long before that point, and that the business of being a werewolf hews pragmatic tends to mean they don't often get caught in the esoterica of reality. In the same way most werewolves would go &quot;huh, neat&quot; and then go back to business with minimal adjustmnent on learning they used to rule a city in Sumer or all the details of the Sundered World, &quot;Enlightenment&quot;, whatever that means and looks like for werewolves, is not usually a thing of interest to most of them. As always, though, there's probably a lodge that takes it deathly serious.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, I mentioned before that when I get into higher power werewolf characters, I tend to make them Lone Wolves from the Chronicler's Guide, and that's because that's what I mostly imagine an escalated form of werewolves would look like-able to do the work of a whole pack on their own, totem and head of a spirit court in their own right, hyper powerful Auspices, stuff like that feels right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-13T04:20:56-08:00","id":1496973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496753-bodhisattva-predator-arcana-werewolves?p=1496871#post1496871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of them initially showed up as Enlightenments in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/798541-alpha-predators-the-strongest-werewolves?p=801351#post801351\">Chris Allen's writeup of Lycaon-Ur as a werewolf</a>. Others include being able to run tirelessly at the speed of the day's change (in practical terms, this translates to about a thousand miles per hour), negate any impediment to getting your teeth into an enemy, or come back from the dead fully healed once per scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides Lycaon-Ur, I also found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/444409-milestone-gifts-in-2e\"><b>this homebrew</b></a>. It might work as a point of reference for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27672-forsakenprospects\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27672_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27672\" data-vbnamecard=\"27672\">ForsakenProspects</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby"